 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "The constructible derived category",
 "statement": "Let $\\mathcal A=\\mathrm{Mod}_\\Lambda$ with $\\Lambda$ a finite ring. The\nfull subcategory $D^b_c(\\et X)$ of the bounded derived category\n$D^b(\\shv{\\et X})$ consisting of the complexes all of whose cohomology\nsheaves are constructible is a triangulated subcategory.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/prop-constructible-derived-subcategory.md",
  "place": "node prop-constructible-derived-subcategory, order 1523"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-constant",
  "def-constructible-constructible",
  "def-constructible-finite",
  "def-constructible-finite-locally-constant",
  "def-constructible-locally-constant",
  "def-constructible-stratification",
  "def-kun-separably-closed"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For a weak Serre subcategory $\\mathcal C$ of an abelian category, the\ncomplexes with cohomology in $\\mathcal C$ form a triangulated subcategory\nof the derived category: the zero object and shifts are clear, and for a\ndistinguished triangle $K\\to L\\to M\\to K[1]$ with $K$ and $M$ having\ncohomology in $\\mathcal C$, the long exact cohomology sequence\n$H^{n}(K)\\to H^n(L)\\to H^n(M)$ exhibits $H^n(L)$ as an extension of a\nsubobject of $H^n(M)$ (a kernel) by a quotient of $H^n(K)$ (a cokernel),\nboth in $\\mathcal C$, hence $H^n(L)\\in\\mathcal C$. Apply this to the weak\nSerre subcategory of [thm-constructible-serre]. (In the formalisation the\ngeneral statement is `DerivedCategory.homologyProperty_isTriangulated`, for any\nproperty of objects closed under isomorphisms, kernels, cokernels and extensions; it is\napplied to the constructible sheaves with these closure properties, the content of\n[thm-constructible-serre], as hypotheses.)",
   "uses": [
    "thm-constructible-serre"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
